@startuml SQLGenie_MCP_Sequence_Workflow
!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 2
skinparam roundcorner 20
skinparam maxmessagesize 60

title SQLGenie MCP Integration - Detailed Sequence Workflow

actor User as user
participant "Claude Desktop\nUI" as ui
participant "Claude AI\nEngine" as claude
participant "MCP Client" as mcpClient
participant "mcp_server.py" as mcpServer
participant "DatabaseManager" as dbManager
participant "SQLite Database" as db
participant "Schema Cache" as cache

== MCP Server Initialization ==

note over user : User starts MCP server:\npython mcp_server.py

mcpServer -> mcpServer : Initialize DatabaseManager
mcpServer -> db : Scan data/sakila.db
mcpServer -> db : Scan data/uploaded_databases/
mcpServer -> cache : Load cached schemas
mcpServer -> mcpServer : **MCP Server Ready**\nListening on stdio

note over mcpServer : Server waiting for\nClaude Desktop connections

== Claude Desktop Connection ==

user -> ui : Opens Claude Desktop
ui -> claude : Initialize session
claude -> mcpClient : Load MCP servers from config
mcpClient -> mcpServer : **MCP Initialize Request**\n{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "method": "initialize"}
mcpServer -> mcpClient : **Initialize Response**\n{"capabilities": {"tools": {...}}}
mcpClient -> mcpServer : **List Tools Request**\n{"method": "tools/list"}
mcpServer -> mcpClient : **Available Tools Response**\n["list_databases", "get_database_schema",\n"execute_sql_query", "analyze_query_results"]

note over claude, mcpServer : **MCP Connection Established**

== User Query: "What databases do I have?" ==

user -> ui : **"What databases do I have available?"**
ui -> claude : Natural language input
claude -> claude : **Intent Analysis:**\n"User wants to see available databases"

claude -> mcpClient : **Tool Selection Decision**
mcpClient -> mcpServer : **MCP Tool Call**\n{"method": "tools/call",\n"params": {"name": "list_databases", "arguments": {}}}

mcpServer -> dbManager : **list_databases()**
dbManager -> db : Check data/sakila.db exists
db -> dbManager : ✓ Found (5.8MB)
dbManager -> db : Scan data/uploaded_databases/
db -> dbManager : ✓ Found sample_company.db
dbManager -> cache : Read cached metadata
cache -> dbManager : Schema info & table counts

dbManager -> mcpServer : **Database List**\n[{"id": "sakila", "name": "Sakila Database",\n"tables": 16, "size": "5.8MB"},\n{"id": "sample_company", "tables": 5}]
mcpServer -> mcpClient : **MCP Tool Response**\n{"result": {"databases": [...], "total_count": 2}}
mcpClient -> claude : Structured database data

claude -> claude : **Format User Response**
claude -> ui : **"You have 2 databases available:\n\n1. **Sakila Database** (16 tables) - Movie rental sample\n2. **Sample Company** (5 tables) - Business data\n\nWould you like to explore any of these?"**
ui -> user : Display formatted response

== User Query: "Show me the Sakila database schema" ==

user -> ui : **"Show me the structure of the sakila database"**
ui -> claude : Natural language input
claude -> claude : **Intent Analysis:**\n"User wants detailed schema for sakila"

claude -> mcpClient : **Tool Selection Decision**
mcpClient -> mcpServer : **MCP Tool Call**\n{"method": "tools/call",\n"params": {"name": "get_database_schema",\n"arguments": {"database_id": "sakila"}}}

mcpServer -> dbManager : **get_database_schema("sakila")**
dbManager -> cache : Check cached schema for sakila
cache -> dbManager : Cache valid (less than 24h old)

alt Schema Cache Hit
    cache -> dbManager : **Complete Schema Data**\n{"tables": {"actor": {...}, "film": {...}}}
else Schema Cache Miss
    dbManager -> db : **PRAGMA table_info(actor)**
    db -> dbManager : actor_id, first_name, last_name, last_update
    dbManager -> db : **PRAGMA table_info(film)**
    db -> dbManager : film_id, title, description, release_year...
    dbManager -> db : **PRAGMA foreign_key_list(rental)**
    db -> dbManager : customer_id -> customer(customer_id)
    
    loop for each table (16 tables)
        dbManager -> db : Get table structure & relationships
        db -> dbManager : Column details + foreign keys
    end
    
    dbManager -> cache : **Store complete schema**
    cache -> dbManager : ✓ Cached with timestamp
end

dbManager -> mcpServer : **Complete Schema Response**\n{"database_id": "sakila",\n"tables": {...}, "relationships": {...}}

mcpServer -> mcpClient : **MCP Tool Response**\n{"result": {"schema": {...}}}
mcpClient -> claude : Structured schema data

claude -> claude : **Analyze & Format Schema**
claude -> ui : **"The Sakila database contains 16 interconnected tables:\n\n**Core Tables:**\n• **actor** (4 columns) - Actor information\n• **film** (13 columns) - Movie details\n• **customer** (8 columns) - Customer data\n• **rental** (7 columns) - Rental transactions\n\n**Relationships:**\n• Films have actors (film_actor junction)\n• Customers make rentals\n• Rentals involve inventory items\n\nWould you like to query any of this data?"**
ui -> user : Display schema overview

== User Query: "Find customers from California" ==

user -> ui : **"Find all customers from California"**
ui -> claude : Natural language input
claude -> claude : **SQL Generation:**\n"Need to join customer, address, city, country\nto filter by state/country"

claude -> mcpClient : **Tool Selection Decision**
mcpClient -> mcpServer : **MCP Tool Call**\n{"method": "tools/call",\n"params": {"name": "execute_sql_query",\n"arguments": {"database_id": "sakila",\n"query": "SELECT c.first_name, c.last_name, a.address, ci.city\nFROM customer c\nJOIN address a ON c.address_id = a.address_id\nJOIN city ci ON a.city_id = ci.city_id\nJOIN country co ON ci.country_id = co.country_id\nWHERE co.country = 'United States'\nAND a.district LIKE '%California%'"}}}

mcpServer -> dbManager : **execute_query("sakila", sql)**
dbManager -> dbManager : **Security Validation**\n• ✓ Read-only query (SELECT)\n• ✓ Query length < 10,000 chars\n• ✓ No dangerous operations\n• ✓ Valid syntax

dbManager -> db : **Execute Query**\n"SELECT c.first_name, c.last_name..."
db -> dbManager : **Query Results**\n[{"first_name": "Mary", "last_name": "Smith",\n"address": "1913 Hanoi Way", "city": "Sasebo"},\n{"first_name": "Patricia", ...}, ...]

dbManager -> dbManager : **Apply Result Limits**\n• Limit to 1000 rows max\n• Check result size

dbManager -> mcpServer : **Query Results**\n{"success": true, "results": [...],\n"row_count": 9, "columns": [...]}

mcpServer -> mcpClient : **MCP Tool Response**
mcpClient -> claude : Query results data

claude -> mcpClient : **Follow-up Analysis**
mcpClient -> mcpServer : **MCP Tool Call**\n{"method": "tools/call",\n"params": {"name": "analyze_query_results",\n"arguments": {"query": "...", "results": [...]}}}

mcpServer -> dbManager : **analyze_query_results()**
dbManager -> dbManager : **Generate Insights**\n• Count by city\n• Identify patterns\n• Create summary

dbManager -> mcpServer : **Analysis Response**\n{"insights": "Found 9 customers in California",\n"patterns": ["Most from Los Angeles area"],\n"summary": "Customer distribution analysis"}

mcpServer -> mcpClient : **Analysis Tool Response**
mcpClient -> claude : Analysis data

claude -> claude : **Combine Results + Analysis**
claude -> ui : **"I found 9 customers from California:\n\n[Table showing customer details]\n\n**Insights:**\n• Most customers are in the Los Angeles area\n• Good geographic distribution\n• All have active rental history\n\nWould you like to see their rental patterns?"**
ui -> user : Display results with insights

== Security Example: Dangerous Query Blocked ==

user -> ui : **"Delete all customer data"**
ui -> claude : Natural language input
claude -> claude : **SQL Generation:**\n"DELETE FROM customer" (dangerous!)

claude -> mcpClient : **Tool Selection Decision**
mcpClient -> mcpServer : **MCP Tool Call**\n{"method": "tools/call",\n"params": {"name": "execute_sql_query",\n"arguments": {"query": "DELETE FROM customer"}}}

mcpServer -> dbManager : **execute_query(dangerous_sql)**
dbManager -> dbManager : **Security Validation FAILED**\n• ❌ DELETE operation detected\n• ❌ Not in allowed operations\n• ❌ Potentially dangerous

dbManager -> mcpServer : **Security Error**\n{"success": false,\n"error": "Dangerous operation blocked",\n"error_type": "SecurityError",\n"allowed_operations": ["SELECT", "WITH", "PRAGMA", "EXPLAIN"]}

mcpServer -> mcpClient : **Error Response**
mcpClient -> claude : Security error information

claude -> claude : **Handle Security Limitation**
claude -> ui : **"I can't perform DELETE operations for security.\nI'm restricted to read-only operations (SELECT queries).\n\nI can help you:\n• View customer data\n• Analyze customer patterns\n• Export customer information\n\nWould you like me to show you the customer data instead?"**
ui -> user : Helpful security explanation

note over user, db : **MCP Security Features:**\n• Read-only operations only\n• Query validation & sanitization\n• Result size limits (1000 rows)\n• Query timeout (30 seconds)\n• Dangerous operation blocking\n• Input length validation

@enduml